From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] shaders: a saved preset wins over --set-shader

--set-shader is meant to work like a global auto-shader, as the comment
over this code says, but it won outright: with a --set-shader path the
driver could load, game, folder, core and global presets were never
looked for. A launcher passing the system's shader at every start, as
ours does, made saving a preset from the menu look broken - the file
was written and never loaded.

Look for a saved preset first and fall back to --set-shader.

Tested on SM8550 (Retroid Pocket Nova), Super Mario World started with
--set-shader crt-guest-advanced and a game preset referencing the Game
Boy shader: before, crt-guest-advanced loaded and the preset was never
found; after, "Shader preset found" and the Game Boy passes compiled.
With the preset removed, crt-guest-advanced loads as before.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
diff --git a/gfx/video_shader_parse.c b/gfx/video_shader_parse.c
--- a/gfx/video_shader_parse.c
+++ b/gfx/video_shader_parse.c
@@ -4163,27 +4163,24 @@ const char *video_shader_get_current_shader_preset(void)
 
       video_driver_modify_disp_flags(0, VIDEO_FLAG_SHADER_PRESETS_NEED_RELOAD);
 
-      if (BIT32_GET(flags.flags,
-               video_shader_type_to_flag(video_shader_parse_type(video_st->cli_shader_path))))
-         strlcpy(runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path,
-               video_st->cli_shader_path,
-               sizeof(runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path));
-      else
-      {
-         if (auto_shaders_enable) /* sets runtime_shader_preset_path */
-         {
-            if (video_shader_load_auto_shader_preset(
+      /* A preset the player saved - game, folder, core or global -
+       * comes first, as the comment above says. The --set-shader path
+       * used to win outright, so with a launcher passing one at every
+       * start a saved preset was written and never loaded. */
+      if (     auto_shaders_enable /* sets runtime_shader_preset_path */
+            && video_shader_load_auto_shader_preset(
                      settings->paths.directory_video_shader,
                      settings->paths.directory_menu_config,
                      runloop_st->system.info.library_name,
                      runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path,
                      sizeof(runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path)))
-            {
-               RARCH_LOG("[Shaders] Shader preset found at \"%s\".\n",
-                     runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path);
-            }
-         }
-      }
+         RARCH_LOG("[Shaders] Shader preset found at \"%s\".\n",
+               runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path);
+      else if (BIT32_GET(flags.flags,
+               video_shader_type_to_flag(video_shader_parse_type(video_st->cli_shader_path))))
+         strlcpy(runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path,
+               video_st->cli_shader_path,
+               sizeof(runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path));
       return runloop_st->runtime_shader_preset_path;
    }
 
